{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1551544-advice-on-a-storyline-involving-the-beast-courts","id":1551544,"title":"Advice on a storyline involving the Beast Courts","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2025-06-09T11:57:41-07:00","id":1551544,"title":"Advice on a storyline involving the Beast Courts","content":"Had a fun storyline idea for a future Werewolf campaign set in a timeline where the Final Battle is rapidly approaching and the Veil is starting to collapse when Fomori become public knowledge, and being treated like a viral plague by a increasingly paranoid government, who don't know the true origins of the monsters.<br /> Garou fighting against HARP, an Authoritarian government backed paramilitary organization's activities in California and the Pacific Northwest have recently found that the normal methods of offering money and other benefits to local Resistance cells are becoming harder and harder. They soon discover that emissaries from local representatives of the Beast Courts in San Francisco and other cities are offering money and other benefits to local cells, and they seem to be snapping it up.<br /> <br /> I need advice on thinking up the motivations of the Beast Courts,besides wanting to help fight off a Authoritarian agency and what exactly they are offering the Cells, any advice on how to make this work?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12186,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12186-killerclown","user":"Killerclown","date":".  Typos 06-09-2025, 02:58 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12186-killerclown","name":"Killerclown","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"819"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-06-18T17:44:52-07:00","id":1551762,"title":"","content":"I can think of a few options.<br /> <br /> 1. The Beast Courts want concessions from the Garou, either now or in the post-war order they think is going to come. Maybe there's a caern they want the Garou to drop their claims to, maybe there's artifacts or fetishes they want returned, maybe it's something else entirely. They're trying to build their influence in North America as a bargaining chip. If the Garou are cooperative, the Garou get the full help of those cells--and the Beast Courts themselves.<br /> 2. The Beast Courts want to expand. They've absorbed Garou tribes before. In their view the Apocalypse War should be conducted largely under their leadership. As they are a multi-species organization with a long history, they can best direct all of Gaia's protectors. Depending on the terms and relative power of each organization, the Garou of the region might be well advised to take the deal.<br /> 3. The Beast Courts have secretly broken the Veil and are working with government elements, take your pick of which--could be state or city governments that want to secede, could be foreign backers, could be both. In addition to their interests in fighting a government agency at odds to them, they're trying to strengthen their mortal allies.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28383-citrakayah","name":"Citrakayah","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar28383_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"101"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}